{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>But only in the place that YHWH will choose in one of your tribes.</b> The verse leaves it unspecified and does not identify which of the tribes, and this was in the portion of Binyamin. Above it mentions 'in all your tribes' — how so? When David bought the threshing-floor from Aravnah the Jebusite, he collected the gold from all the tribes, as it is written in Divrei HaYamim (I 21): ״ויתן דויד לארנן במקום שקלי זהב משקל שש מאות״, and it is written in Sefer Shmuel (II 24): ״ויקן דויד את הגרן ואת הבקר בכסף שקלים חמשים״. These two verses appear to contradict each other, but it is not so, for the six hundred were for the twelve tribes — fifty for each and every tribe — and the fifty mentioned here was for his own tribe, which was the tribe of Yehudah. In any event, this threshing-floor was in the portion of Binyamin."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:53.442207903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}